D("2026-10-31","Reformation Day","The King Who Found the Book","an older kid","Psalm 119:11",[(11,"I have stored up your word in my heart, that I might not sin against you.")],
"Josiah’s reformation",[
"Long before Martin Luther, there was a reformation right in the Bible. Josiah became king of Judah when he was only eight years old. The kings before him had worshiped idols and forgotten God, and the temple in Jerusalem had fallen apart.",
"When Josiah grew up, he told workers to repair the temple. While they were cleaning, the high priest found something dusty in a back room: the Book of the Law, God’s Word that had been lost for years! They read it to the king. When Josiah heard it, he tore his robes. “We have not been doing what God says!”",
"Josiah gathered all the people, young and old, and read the whole book out loud to them. Then he promised to follow the Lord with all his heart. He tore down the idols, cleaned out the temple, and held the biggest Passover celebration in hundreds of years. God’s Word, found again, changed a whole nation, just like it did in Luther’s day."],
"Reformation Day",["“Reformation” means being formed again around God’s Word. It happened with Josiah, it happened with Luther, and it happens in us every time we hear God’s Word and turn back to Him."],
["How old was Josiah when he became king? What did the workers find in the temple?","Why did Josiah tear his robes when he heard God’s Word?","How can God’s Word get “lost” in our lives, even when we own a Bible?"],
"Lord God, thank You for giving us Your Word, and for leaders like Josiah and Luther who helped people find it again.","Help us store up Your Word in our hearts.",
"King Josiah found God’s lost book in the temple and read it to all the people. God’s Word changed everything!",
["Josiah became king when he was [eight].","Workers found the Book of the [Law].","Josiah tore his [robes].","He read the book to all the [people].","Today is [Reformation] Day."],
["JOSIAH","BOOK","TEMPLE","KING","WORD","LAW"],[("Was God’s Word lost in the temple?",["Yes","No"],0),("What did Josiah do with the idols?",["Tore them down","Kept them"],0)],
"Draw King Josiah holding the book that was found.",("Psalm 119:11","“I have stored up your word in my heart.”"),
scene(temple(),scroll(320,236),person(150,beard=True,arms="open",hair="short"),crown(150,114),person(500,beard=True,arms="mixed",hair="wrap"),label="Coloring picture: King Josiah at the temple with the found scroll"))

D("2026-11-01","All Saints’ Day","Lazarus, Come Out!","Mom or Dad","John 11:25–26",[(25,"Jesus said to her, “I am the resurrection and the life. Whoever believes in me, though he die, yet shall he live,"),(26,"and everyone who lives and believes in me shall never die. Do you believe this?”")],
"Jesus raises Lazarus",[
"Jesus had three dear friends: Mary, Martha, and their brother Lazarus. One day Lazarus got very sick, and the sisters sent word to Jesus. But by the time Jesus arrived, Lazarus had died and had been in the tomb for four days.",
"Martha ran to meet Jesus. “Lord, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.” Jesus told her, “I am the resurrection and the life. Whoever believes in Me, though he die, yet shall he live.” Then Jesus went to the tomb, and He cried. Jesus loved His friend.",
"Jesus said, “Take away the stone.” Then He prayed and shouted in a loud voice, “Lazarus, come out!” And Lazarus walked out of the tomb, still wrapped in burial cloths! Jesus said, “Unbind him, and let him go.” Death had to obey Jesus."],
"All Saints’ Day",["Today we remember Christians who have died and are now with Jesus. Death is real and it is sad. Jesus cried too. But it isn’t the end. The same voice that called Lazarus will call all believers out of their graves on the Last Day."],
["What did Jesus shout at the tomb? Why did Jesus cry?","What did Jesus tell Martha about who He is?","How does Jesus being “the resurrection and the life” change how Christians grieve?"],
"Lord Jesus, You are the resurrection and the life. Thank You for all Your saints who now rest with You, and for the people we love who have died in the faith.","Comfort everyone who is sad, and keep us in faith until we see them again.",
"Jesus called His friend Lazarus out of the tomb! On All Saints’ Day we remember that Jesus is stronger than death.",
["Lazarus had two sisters, Mary and [Martha].","Lazarus was in the tomb for four [days].","Jesus [cried] because He loved Lazarus.","Jesus said, “Lazarus, come [out]!”","Jesus is the resurrection and the [life]."],
["LAZARUS","TOMB","LIFE","SAINTS","MARTHA","STONE"],[("Did Lazarus come out of the tomb?",["Yes","No"],0),("Who is stronger than death?",["Jesus","Nobody"],0)],
"Draw Lazarus walking out of the tomb.",("John 11:25","“I am the resurrection and the life.”"),
scene(hills(),'<path d="M380,300 V190 Q480,120 580,190 V300 Z"/><path d="M440,300 V240 a40,40 0 0 1 80,0 V300" />','<circle cx="600" cy="262" r="38"/>',person(200,beard=True,arms="up",hair="short"),person(470,beard=False,arms="open",hair="wrap",s=.8),sun(80,60),label="Coloring picture: Jesus calling Lazarus out of the tomb"))

S="In the Beginning"
D("2026-11-02",S,"God Made Everything","a K–2nd grader, with help","Genesis 1:1, 31",[(1,"In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth."),(31,"And God saw everything that he had made, and behold, it was very good. And there was evening and there was morning, the sixth day.")],
"Creation",[
"In the very beginning, there was nothing at all: no sky, no ground, no people, not even light. Only God. Then God spoke. “Let there be light,” and there was light! On the first day God made day and night.",
"Day by day, God kept speaking, and everything He said happened. He made the sky and the waters. He made dry land with trees, flowers, and fruit. He hung the sun, the moon, and the stars. He filled the seas with fish and the sky with birds. He made animals of every kind: lions, ladybugs, elephants, and puppies.",
"On the sixth day, God did something special. He made a man, Adam, from the dust of the ground and breathed life into him. Then He made a woman, Eve. God made people in His own image, to know Him and love Him. God looked at everything He had made, and it was very good. On the seventh day, God rested."],
"Very good",["God made everything out of nothing, just by speaking. That means everything belongs to Him, including us. Luther’s explanation of the First Article says, “I believe that God has made me and all creatures.” You are not an accident. God made you on purpose."],
["What did God make on the first day? What is your favorite thing God made?","How did God make everything? What made people different from animals?","What does it mean that you were made in God’s image? How should that change how we treat other people?"],
"Creator God, thank You for making the whole world and for making each of us. Everything You made is good.","Help us take care of Your world and thank You for it.",
"God made everything just by speaking, and it was very good!",
["In the beginning, God [created] the heavens and the earth.","On the first day God made [light].","God made the first man, [Adam].","God made people in His own [image].","On the seventh day God [rested]."],
["CREATED","LIGHT","ADAM","EVE","STARS","GOOD"],[("Did God make the world out of nothing?",["Yes","No"],0),("How did God make the world?",["By speaking","By accident"],0)],
"Draw your favorite thing God made.",("Genesis 1:1","“In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth.”"),
scene(sun(90,60),moon(560,50),stars(8,4,(60,520)),hills(),tree(120),tree(530,140),sheep(250),sheep(400,.8),fish(300,120),cloud(330,60),label="Coloring picture: God’s creation with sun, moon, trees, and animals"))

D("2026-11-03",S,"The First Promise","a 3rd–5th grader","Genesis 3:15",[(15,"I will put enmity between you and the woman, and between your offspring and her offspring; he shall bruise your head, and you shall bruise his heel.”")],
"The fall",[
"God put Adam and Eve in a beautiful garden called Eden. They could eat from every tree except one: the tree of the knowledge of good and evil. “If you eat from that one,” God said, “you will die.”",
"One day the devil, disguised as a serpent, spoke to Eve. “Did God really say that? You won’t die. You’ll be like God!” Eve looked at the fruit. It looked so good. She ate some and gave some to Adam, and he ate too. Right away they felt ashamed and hid from God among the trees.",
"God came walking in the garden. “Where are you?” Adam blamed Eve, and Eve blamed the serpent. Sin had come into the world, and now there would be pain and death. But God, even then, made a promise. He told the serpent that one day a child of the woman would crush his head. That was the very first promise of Jesus, who would defeat the devil on the cross."],
"The first promise",["Sin made Adam and Eve hide from God. Sin still makes us want to hide and blame others. But God didn’t leave them. He came looking for them and gave them a promise. God always comes looking for us too."],
["What did the serpent say to Eve? What did Adam and Eve do after they ate?","Who did Adam blame? Who did Eve blame? Why do we blame others when we do wrong?","Genesis 3:15 is called the “first Gospel.” How does it point to Jesus?"],
"Lord God, we are sorry that we sin like Adam and Eve. Thank You for coming to look for us, and for sending Jesus to crush the devil.","When we want to hide or blame, help us come to You and confess.",
"Adam and Eve ate the fruit God said not to eat. But God promised a Savior who would crush the serpent!",
["God put Adam and Eve in the garden of [Eden].","The devil came as a [serpent].","After they sinned, they [hid] from God.","God promised a child who would crush the serpent’s [head].","That child is [Jesus]."],
["EDEN","SERPENT","FRUIT","PROMISE","GARDEN","JESUS"],[("Did God stop loving Adam and Eve?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who would crush the serpent?",["Jesus","Adam"],0)],
"Draw the garden of Eden.",("Genesis 3:15","“He shall bruise your head.”"),
scene(tree(320,190),'<path d="M290,240 q-40,10 -20,30 q30,20 60,0 q20,-14 -10,-24" fill="none" stroke-width="7"/><ellipse cx="338" cy="238" rx="10" ry="7"/>','<circle cx="300" cy="150" r="9"/><circle cx="350" cy="160" r="9"/>',person(160,beard=True,arms="mixed",hair="short"),person(480,beard=False,arms="open",hair="curly"),label="Coloring picture: Adam and Eve in the garden by the tree"))

D("2026-11-04",S,"Noah and the Rainbow","an older kid","Genesis 9:13",[(13,"I have set my bow in the cloud, and it shall be a sign of the covenant between me and the earth.")],
"Noah’s ark",[
"After Adam and Eve, the world filled up with people, and they got worse and worse. Everyone did evil all the time. God was sad that He had made people. But one man, Noah, trusted God.",
"God told Noah, “Build a giant boat, an ark, because I am going to send a flood.” Noah obeyed, even though people probably laughed at him. When the ark was finished, God sent animals two by two, and Noah’s family went inside. Then God Himself shut the door. It rained forty days and forty nights until water covered even the mountains. But everyone inside the ark was safe.",
"After many months, the water went down. Noah sent out a dove, and it came back with an olive leaf. At last the ark rested on dry ground, and everyone came out. Noah thanked God, and God put a rainbow in the sky. “I will never again destroy the earth with a flood,” He promised. Every rainbow is God keeping His promise."],
"Safe in the ark",["The ark saved Noah’s family through the water. 1 Peter 3 says Baptism is like that: God saves us through water and puts us safe inside His Church. And every time you see a rainbow, God is reminding you that He keeps His promises."],
["How many of each animal went into the ark? Who shut the door?","Why do you think people laughed at Noah? Why did he keep building?","1 Peter 3:20–21 connects the flood with Baptism. How is Baptism like the ark?"],
"Faithful God, thank You for keeping Noah safe in the ark, and for keeping us safe in Your family through Baptism.","When we see a rainbow, help us remember that You always keep Your promises.",
"God kept Noah’s family safe in the ark and put a rainbow in the sky as a promise!",
["Noah built an [ark].","The animals came in two by [two].","It rained forty [days] and forty nights.","The dove brought back an olive [leaf].","God’s promise sign is the [rainbow]."],
["NOAH","ARK","RAINBOW","DOVE","FLOOD","ANIMALS"],[("Who shut the door of the ark?",["God","Noah"],0),("Will God flood the whole earth again?",["Yes","No"],1)],
"Draw the ark with animals and a rainbow.",("Genesis 9:13","“I have set my bow in the cloud.”"),
scene(rainbow(),ark(),waves(282),'<path d="M500,90 q14,-14 28,0 q-14,10 -28,0 Z M528,90 l14,-4 l-4,10 Z"/>',label="Coloring picture: Noah’s ark under a rainbow"))

D("2026-11-05",S,"The Tower of Babel","a 3rd–5th grader","Proverbs 16:18; James 4:10",[("Prov 16:18","Pride goes before destruction, and a haughty spirit before a fall."),("James 4:10","Humble yourselves before the Lord, and he will exalt you.")],
"A tower to the sky",[
"After the flood, Noah’s family grew into many families, and they all spoke one language. They settled on a flat plain and had an idea. “Let’s make bricks and build a city with a tower that reaches up to heaven. Then we’ll make a great name for ourselves!”",
"They didn’t want to give glory to God. They wanted glory for themselves. So they baked bricks and stacked them higher and higher. But God came down to see their tower. He said, “If they do this, nothing will stop them from doing whatever proud thing they want.”",
"So God mixed up their language. Suddenly one person said “Pass the bricks,” and the other heard nonsense! Nobody could understand anyone. They had to stop building, and they spread out over the whole earth. The city was called Babel, because there God confused their language."],
"Pride and humility",["Pride says, “Look at me.” Faith says, “Look at God.” Many years later, on Pentecost, God did the opposite of Babel: the apostles spoke and everyone heard the good news of Jesus in their own language. God brings people back together in Jesus."],
["What were the people building? What did God do to their language?","Why did the people want to build the tower? What does it mean to be proud?","How is Pentecost (Acts 2) like Babel turned upside down? Where do you see people trying to “make a name” for themselves?"],
"Heavenly Father, forgive us when we are proud and want glory for ourselves. Thank You for Jesus, who humbled Himself for us.","Teach us to give You the glory in everything we do.",
"The people built a tall tower to make themselves famous. God mixed up their language, and they had to stop!",
["The people built a tall [tower].","They made it out of [bricks].","They wanted to make a name for [themselves].","God mixed up their [language].","The city was called [Babel]."],
["BABEL","TOWER","BRICKS","PRIDE","HUMBLE","LANGUAGE"],[("Were the people giving glory to God?",["Yes","No"],1),("Pride goes before a…",["Fall","Party"],0)],
"Draw the tower of Babel, and people who can’t understand each other.",("James 4:10","“Humble yourselves before the Lord.”"),
scene(wall(250,390,60),'<path d="M240,300 H400 M260,60 H380"/>',person(130,beard=True,arms="mixed",hair="short",s=.8),person(500,beard=False,arms="open",hair="wrap",s=.8),'<path d="M90,150 q20,-20 40,0 l-6,12 Z M520,140 q20,-20 40,0 l-6,12 Z" />','<text x="98" y="150" style="font:700 16px sans-serif;stroke:none;fill:#1c1c1a">?!</text><text x="528" y="140" style="font:700 16px sans-serif;stroke:none;fill:#1c1c1a">??</text>',label="Coloring picture: the tower of Babel with confused builders"))

D("2026-11-06",S,"God Will Provide","an older kid","Genesis 22:8",[(8,"Abraham said, “God will provide for himself the lamb for a burnt offering, my son.” So they went both of them together.")],
"Abraham and Isaac",[
"Remember Abraham, who counted the stars? God finally gave him and Sarah a son, Isaac, the promised child. Abraham loved him very much. Then one day God tested Abraham. “Take your son, your only son Isaac, whom you love, and offer him as a sacrifice on a mountain I will show you.”",
"Abraham’s heart must have been breaking, but he trusted God. He got up early, and he and Isaac climbed the mountain. Isaac carried the wood on his back. “Father,” Isaac said, “here is the fire and the wood, but where is the lamb?” Abraham answered, “God will provide the lamb, my son.”",
"At the top, Abraham built an altar and laid Isaac on it. But just then the angel of the Lord called out, “Abraham! Don’t hurt the boy! Now I know you trust God.” Abraham looked up, and there was a ram caught by its horns in a bush. God had provided! Abraham named the place “The Lord Will Provide.”"],
"The Lamb God provides",["This story points straight to Jesus. Isaac carried wood up a mountain; Jesus carried a wooden cross up a hill. God spared Isaac, but He did not spare His own Son. Jesus is the Lamb God provided for us, as John the Baptist said: “Behold, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!”"],
["What did Isaac carry up the mountain? What did God provide instead of Isaac?","Why do you think God tested Abraham? How did Abraham show he trusted God?","List the ways Isaac’s story looks like Jesus’ story. Where is the big difference?"],
"Heavenly Father, thank You for providing the ram for Abraham, and for providing Jesus, the Lamb of God, for us.","When we can’t see how things will work out, help us trust that You will provide.",
"God tested Abraham, and then provided a ram instead of Isaac. God provided Jesus, the Lamb, for us!",
["Abraham’s son was named [Isaac].","Isaac carried the [wood].","Abraham said, “God will [provide].”","God sent a [ram] caught in a bush.","Jesus is the [Lamb] of God."],
["ABRAHAM","ISAAC","RAM","PROVIDE","LAMB","ALTAR"],[("Did God let Abraham hurt Isaac?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who is the Lamb God provided for us?",["Jesus","Isaac"],0)],
"Draw the ram caught in the bush.",("Genesis 22:8","“God will provide for himself the lamb.”"),
scene(mountains(),altar(320),person(170,beard=True,arms="up",hair="wrap"),person(460,beard=False,arms="open",hair="short",s=.75),ram(560),label="Coloring picture: Abraham, Isaac, the altar, and the ram"))

D("2026-11-07",S,"Jacob’s Ladder","a 3rd–5th grader","Genesis 28:15",[(15,"Behold, I am with you and will keep you wherever you go, and will bring you back to this land. For I will not leave you until I have done what I have promised you.”")],
"A stairway to heaven",[
"Isaac grew up and had twin sons, Esau and Jacob. Jacob tricked his brother and his father to get the family blessing, and Esau was so angry that Jacob had to run away from home. He ran far into the wilderness, all alone.",
"That night, Jacob used a stone for a pillow and fell asleep. He had an amazing dream: a stairway reaching from the ground all the way up to heaven, with God’s angels going up and down on it. And at the top stood the Lord Himself.",
"God said, “I am the God of Abraham and Isaac. I will give you this land and many children, and through your family all the earth will be blessed. I am with you and will keep you wherever you go.” Jacob woke up and said, “Surely the Lord is in this place, and I did not know it!” God made that promise to a runaway who didn’t deserve it."],
"God is with you",["Jacob had messed up badly, and he was alone and afraid. God didn’t come to scold him. He came with a promise. Jesus later said He Himself is the ladder (John 1:51): He connects heaven and earth, and brings God to us."],
["What did Jacob use for a pillow? What was on the stairway?","Why was Jacob running away? Did he deserve God’s promise?","Jesus said He is like Jacob’s ladder (John 1:51). What did He mean?"],
"Lord God, thank You for being with Jacob even when he ran away, and for being with us wherever we go.","When we feel alone, remind us that You are with us.",
"Jacob ran away and slept on a stone. God showed him a stairway to heaven and promised, “I am with you.”",
["Jacob’s twin brother was [Esau].","Jacob used a [stone] for a pillow.","He dreamed of a [stairway] to heaven.","Angels went up and [down].","God said, “I am [with] you.”"],
["JACOB","LADDER","ANGELS","DREAM","STONE","HEAVEN"],[("Did Jacob deserve God’s promise?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who connects heaven and earth?",["Jesus","Jacob"],0)],
"Draw Jacob’s stairway with angels on it.",("Genesis 28:15","“I am with you and will keep you wherever you go.”"),
scene(stars(16,9,(260,420)),moon(80,60),'<path d="M290,300 L330,40 M370,300 L410,40" fill="none" stroke-width="3"/>'+''.join(f'<path d="M{290+k*4},{300-k*26} H{370+k*4}" fill="none" stroke-width="2"/>' for k in range(10)),angel(470,.55),angel(250,.45),'<ellipse cx="150" cy="292" rx="30" ry="10"/>','<path d="M110,290 q40,-30 90,-4 l-6,10 q-40,-16 -84,0 Z"/>',label="Coloring picture: Jacob asleep under a stairway to heaven with angels"))

D("2026-11-08",S,"How Majestic Is Your Name","Mom or Dad","Psalm 8:1, 3–4",[(1,"O LORD, our Lord, how majestic is your name in all the earth! You have set your glory above the heavens."),(3,"When I look at your heavens, the work of your fingers, the moon and the stars, which you have set in place,"),(4,"what is man that you are mindful of him, and the son of man that you care for him?")],
"David looks at the stars",[
"Many years later, a shepherd boy named David spent long nights in the fields watching his sheep. With no lights anywhere, the sky above him was full of stars. David looked up and thought about how huge God must be to make all that.",
"Then he thought about how small he was. “When I look at the heavens, the work of Your fingers, the moon and the stars… who am I that You even think about me?” But God doesn’t just think about us. He cares for us. He crowned people with glory and gave them His creation to take care of.",
"David wrote his thoughts into a song, Psalm 8. Thousands of years later, we still sing it. And one day, Jesus quoted this psalm when children shouted “Hosanna!” to Him in the temple: “Out of the mouth of babies and infants, you have prepared praise.” God loves to hear even little children praise Him."],
"Big God, small us",["God made billions of stars, and He knows every one by name. And He knows your name too. That’s the wonder of Psalm 8: the God who made everything cares about you."],
["Who wrote Psalm 8? What did he see in the sky?","How does looking at the stars make you feel? Why would God care about people?","Jesus quoted Psalm 8 when children praised Him (Matthew 21:16). Why do you think God loves the praise of children?"],
"O Lord our Lord, how majestic is Your name in all the earth! Thank You for making the stars, and for caring about each of us.","Help us praise You with our whole lives.",
"David looked at the stars and sang, “How majestic is Your name!” The God who made the stars cares about you!",
["David took care of [sheep].","He looked at the moon and the [stars].","God made them with His [fingers].","God [cares] for us.","Psalm 8 says God’s name is [majestic]."],
["DAVID","STARS","MOON","MAJESTIC","PSALM","PRAISE"],[("Does God know your name?",["Yes","No"],0),("Who made the stars?",["God","Nobody"],0)],
"Go outside tonight and look at the stars. Then draw what you see.",("Psalm 8:1","“O LORD, our Lord, how majestic is your name in all the earth!”"),
scene(stars(30,11),moon(560,60),hills(),person(220,beard=False,arms="up",hair="curly"),sheep(380),sheep(470,.8),label="Coloring picture: young David looking at the stars with his sheep"))
